  englishName: Sweet Osmanthus Cake
  chineseName: 桂花糕
  pinyinName: Guihua Gao
  category: 3
  difficulty: 0
  briefDescription: Traditional Chinese pastry made with glutinous rice flour and osmanthus honey.
  detailedDescription: A traditional sweet scent pastry that has been enjoyed in China for hundreds of years. It has a crystal-like appearance and the sweet fragrance of osmanthus flowers.
  historicalOrigin: Legend has it that it originated from the moon goddess Chang'e.
  culturalSymbolism: Eaten during the Mid-Autumn Festival, symbolizing harvest and reunion.
  regionalSignificance: Osmanthus is the city flower of Suzhou.
  craftmanshipNotes: Steaming time is critical for texture.
  estimatedDuration: 300
